Z||000000||kinboyatuwo||11-06-2001||11:53 PM||||First this problem was around before the  work, but has gotten 10X worse now<P>Just replaced the upper control arm bushings and the ball joints on both sides.<P>It feels like the car's rear end is swirving all over the road when it hits a bump (pronounced on the right side).  If i am in a corner it feels sometimes like it wants to go straight while turning and i have to fight the car to stay straight.  Everything in the rear seems tight but one lower ball joint (dont think it is the problem it is not to bad off) feels like a tirerod is not attached but can vow to the fact they are pretty good, the work was done at a GM dealer by PBJ, and i felt this went back and we put it up and couldnt find anything except the balljoint but this cannot be causing it, have had a rear ball joint loose and felt nothing like this<P>any help or ideas<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/b4lower50.jpg"> <BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||11-07-2001||08:11 AM||||Sounds like you need to have a 4-wheel alignment. You should always take the car in for an alignment whenever you change suspension stuff.||||reg||1
